  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 1,
      "char_start": 292,
      "char_end": 669,
      "text": "On the stern, pine-clad southern coast of Norway, off the\npicturesquely-situated town of Arendal, stand planted far out into the\nsea the white walls of the Great and Little Torungen Lighthouses, each\non its bare rock-island of corresponding name, the lesser of which\nseems, as you sail past, to have only just room for the lighthouse and\nthe attendant's residence by the side"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 2,
      "char_start": 844,
      "char_end": 1214,
      "text": "There sat now on the bench by the hearth a lonely old man, of a\nflint-hard and somewhat gloomy countenance, with a mass of white hair\nfalling over his ears and neck, who was generally occupied with some\ncobbling work, and who from time to time, as he drew out the thread,\nwould make some remark aloud, as if he thought he still had the partner\nof his life for audience"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 3,
      "char_start": 272,
      "char_end": 612,
      "text": "All that was known further about \"Old Jacob,\" as he was called, was that\nhe had once been a pilot, and that he had had a son who had taken to\ndrinking, through whose fault it had been eventually that the father had\nlost his certificate; and it was thought that on the occasion in\nquestion the father had taken the son's blame upon himself"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 4,
      "char_start": 654,
      "char_end": 1133,
      "text": "Now and then, when his granddaughter--a\nchild with a thick crop of hair falling about her ears, and a rough dog\nconstantly at her heels--would burst into the house with all the\nfreshness of the outside air blowing round her, as it were, and deliver\nherself of her intelligence, he might be drawn, perhaps, to the window\nto look out over the sea, and afterwards, like a growling bear disturbed\nfrom its lair, even follow her with some difficulty out of the door with\nthe spyglass"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 5,
      "char_start": 1219,
      "char_end": 1446,
      "text": "\"\n\nHe was not going to give up his ascendancy in the matter, hard as she\npushed him; so he bethought him of a pack of old tales there-anent, and\nwent on to explain drily--\n\n\"They go to the Baltic--to Russia--to salt human flesh"
    }
  ],
